</style></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to design</a><div class="shell"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="brand">Morphir / E2</div><div class="meta">Execution and evaluator parity<br>Design revision 0.1 · 1 October 2026</div><nav aria-label="Design sections"><a href="#outcome">01 · One model, reproducible results</a><a href="#baseline">02 · What E1 already provides</a><a href="#pipeline">03 · Follow a call through the pipeline</a><a href="#contracts">04 · Small contracts with explicit ownership</a><a href="#values">05 · Types survive every boundary</a><a href="#ion">06 · Ion profiles and JSON interoperability</a><a href="#adapter">07 · Call the generated public library</a><a href="#targets">08 · Target and host are separate choices</a><a href="#lifecycle">09 · Keep artifacts alive only while needed</a><a href="#oracle">10 · Define what agreement proves</a><a href="#cli">11 · Make execution visible in the engine and CLI</a><a href="#evidence">12 · Evidence that can be checked later</a><a href="#delivery">13 · Deliver complete paths in six slices</a><a href="#decisions">14 · Defaults and boundaries to keep explicit</a><a href="#sources">15 · Implementation references</a></nav></aside><main id="main"><div class="eyebrow">Track 5 · Morphir to Wasm</div><h1>Run the model.<br>Prove the result.</h1><p class="lead">A modular execution pipeline for the MoonBit libraries produced by E1, with typed calls, configurable runtimes and reproducible evaluator comparisons.</p><div class="meta-row"><span class="tag draft">Proposed E2 contracts</span><span class="tag">Baseline fc9cd3c</span><span class="tag">Ion preferred · JSON supported</span></div>
<svg class="hero-art" viewBox="0 0 900 155" role="img" aria-labelledby="hero-title"><title id="hero-title">One model feeds four execution backends and a shared comparison report</title><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor"/></marker></defs><g fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M175 76 H235 M235 20 V132 M235 20 H300 M235 57 H300 M235 94 H300 M235 132 H300 M525 20 H600 M525 57 H600 M525 94 H600 M525 132 H600 M600 20 V132 M600 76 H680" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/></g><g fill="var(--soft)" stroke="var(--line)"><rect x="0" y="42" width="175" height="68" rx="8"/><rect x="300" y="3" width="225" height="33" rx="5"/><rect x="300" y="40" width="225" height="33" rx="5"/><rect x="300" y="77" width="225" height="33" rx="5"/><rect x="300" y="115" width="225" height="33" rx="5"/><rect x="680" y="42" width="215" height="68" rx="8"/></g><g fill="var(--ink)" text-anchor="middle" font-family="system-ui" font-size="16"><text x="87" y="72">Typed model</text><text x="87" y="94">+ call suite</text><text x="412" y="25">Wasm GC</text><text x="412" y="62">Native C</text><text x="412" y="99">Native LLVM</text><text x="412" y="137">JavaScript</text><text x="787" y="72">Compare with evaluator</text><text x="787" y="94">Retain Ion evidence</text></g></svg>
<section id="outcome"><div class="section-no">01 / E2</div><h2>One model, reproducible results</h2>
<p>E2 adds invocation and behavioral verification to the generated libraries delivered by E1. A caller selects public Morphir entry points, supplies typed arguments, and runs the same calls through configured target providers and an evaluator. The engine reports a match, a mismatch, a model error, or a provider failure for each call.</p>
<div class="callout"><strong>Completion means measured parity.</strong><p>A checked-in representative model and call suite must execute through Wasm GC, native C, native LLVM, and JavaScript and agree with the declared evaluator under a versioned comparison policy. Each result binds to the model, calls, generated adapter, compiler, dependencies, runtime, and policy used.</p></div>
<p>Ion remains the preferred engine/intermediate format. Standard Morphir JSON input stays fully supported. A JSON-only evaluator or host adapter uses an explicit, lossless boundary profile; it does not change the rest of the pipeline.</p>
<div class="grid2"><div class="panel"><h3>First useful path</h3><p>Invoke a scalar function with caller-supplied arguments on JavaScript, compare it with the local Scheme evaluator, and return the result through the actual CLI. This establishes the complete path before widening types and targets.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Final E2 acceptance</h3><p>Execute a pricing model with records, custom values, collections, exact arithmetic, closures inside the model, and expected domain errors. Exercise JSON and both Ion encodings, target differences, failed runs, and installed npm packaging.</p></div></div>
</section><section id="baseline"><div class="section-no">02 / E2</div><h2>What E1 already provides</h2>
<p>Baseline: <code>fc9cd3c</code>, the squash merge of <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/31">PR #31</a>. E1 passed 602 tests on each existing test target and its real compiler/CLI acceptance. Those counts describe E1 evidence.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Existing capability</th><th>E2 addition</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Pure generator returns source, manifests, symbols and metadata.</td><td>A separate pure invocation-adapter generator derives typed public entry points from the same IR and symbol mapping.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Compiler acceptance writes a test consumer and runs hard-coded assertions on four targets.</td><td>Reusable caller-supplied calls, explicit outcomes, an evaluator, and structured differential reports.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Library build provider attests to compiler acceptance and deletes its private workspace.</td><td>A session keeps the verified executable alive through bounded execution, then disposes it.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Build receipt binds source, compiler/core, SDK, and build identities.</td><td>Execution receipt additionally binds adapter, executable, invocation, runtime, evaluator and comparison identities.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Target selection accepts native, JS, Wasm, and Wasm GC.</td><td>Distinguish native C from LLVM; negotiate compile and run support independently.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Scheme backend can load a full IR file and call an entry with arguments.</td><td>A typed evaluator adapter with bounded evaluation, normalized errors, and an explicit semantic profile.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recoverable publication replaces a complete task output.</td><td>Publish successful verification evidence only after every required target/call completes; report failed attempts separately.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Existing E1 source-only and build-required commands remain available. E2 does not reinterpret <code>--validation required</code> as execution.</p>
</section><section id="pipeline"><div class="section-no">03 / E2</div><h2>Follow a call through the pipeline</h2><figure class="diagram" id="e2-pipeline"><h3>Data and effect boundaries</h3><div class="diagram-render" aria-label="Data and effect boundaries"><svg id="e2-pipeline-svg" width="100%" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="flowchart" style="max-width: 658.109375px;" viewBox="4 4 658.109375 824" role="graphics-document document" aria-roledescription="flowchart-v2"><style>#e2-pipeline-svg{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:16px;fill:#172c24;}@keyframes edge-animation-frame{from{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}@keyframes dash{to{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-animation-slow{stroke-dasharray:9,5!important;stroke-dashoffset:900;animation:dash 50s linear infinite;stroke-linecap:round;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-animation-fast{stroke-dasharray:9,5!important;stroke-dashoffset:900;animation:dash 20s linear infinite;stroke-linecap:round;}#e2-pipeline-svg .error-icon{fill:#fff;}#e2-pipeline-svg .error-text{fill:#000000;stroke:#000000;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-thickness-normal{stroke-width:1px;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-thickness-thick{stroke-width:3.5px;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-pattern-solid{stroke-dasharray:0;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-thickness-invisible{stroke-width:0;fill:none;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-pattern-dashed{stroke-dasharray:3;}#e2-pipeline-svg .edge-pattern-dotted{stroke-dasharray:2;}#e2-pipeline-svg .marker{fill:#53665e;stroke:#53665e;}#e2-pipeline-svg .marker.cross{stroke:#53665e;}#e2-pipeline-svg svg{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:16px;}#e2-pipeline-svg p{margin:0;}#e2-pipeline-svg .label{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:#172c24;}#e2-pipeline-svg .cluster-label text{fill:#000000;}#e2-pipeline-svg .cluster-label span{color:#000000;}#e2-pipeline-svg .cluster-label span p{background-color:transparent;}#e2-pipeline-svg .label text,#e2-pipeline-svg span{fill:#172c24;color:#172c24;}#e2-pipeline-svg .node rect,#e2-pipeline-svg .node circle