**Interfaces:**
- Consumes: tasks 1 and 2.

- [ ] **Step 1: Tests first.** In `pool.rs` tests, keep the exact-text tests for a start failure and a handshake failure (currently around lines 891-940) unchanged; they must still pass after the side channel goes. Keep the three idle tests (around lines 777-835) and change only their setup to the new sweep.
- [ ] **Step 2: Implement.**
  - `guest.rs` and `extension.rs`: `CallError::Invalid(error)` maps exactly as `Failed` does today. `Connect`/`Handshake` cannot come from a `Session` there; fold them into the wildcard arm.
  - `pool.rs`: delete the `Arc<Mutex<Option<String>>>` side channel; map `CallError::Connect(error)` to the start-failure text and `CallError::Handshake(error)` to the `initialize` failure text the side channel produced. Delete `Activity`, `InUse` and the `in_flight`/`last_used` map; `spawn_idle_sweep` becomes:

    ```rust
    // One extra tick: a guest used just before a tick is evicted n - 1 to n
    // periods later, so + 1 keeps the idle time at least IDLE_LIMIT.
    const IDLE_TICKS: u64 = IDLE_LIMIT.as_secs() / SWEEP_INTERVAL.as_secs() + 1; // 11

    fn spawn_idle_sweep(pool: Weak<Pool<String>>) {
        let Ok(runtime) = tokio::runtime::Handle::try_current() else {
            tracing::warn!("no tokio runtime; idle workbench guests will not be stopped");
            return;
        };
        runtime.spawn(async move {
            let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(SWEEP_INTERVAL);
            interval.tick().await;
            loop {
                interval.tick().await;
                let Some(pool) = pool.upgrade() else { return };
                pool.tick();
                pool.evict_idle(IDLE_TICKS).await;
            }
        });
    }
    ```

  - Update the `PooledInvoker` docs: an idle guest is closed in order; the race note from part 3 goes (eviction skips a slot whose lock is held).
