**Interfaces:**
- Produces:
  ```rust
  /// Warm guests, one per key, reused across calls.
  pub struct Pool<K> { /* async_lock::Mutex<HashMap<K, Arc<Slot>>> */ }
  impl<K: Eq + Hash + Clone + MaybeSend + Sync> Pool<K> {
      pub fn new(config: HostConfig) -> Self;
      /// Call `method` on the guest for `key`, opening it with `open` when there is none,
      /// or when `fingerprint` differs from the cached one. A failed call evicts the guest,
      /// opens a new one, and retries once. A rejected call keeps the guest.
      pub async fn call<P, R, F, Fut>(&self, key: &K, fingerprint: &str, open: F, method: &str, params: &P) -> Result<R, CallError>
      where P: Serialize + Sync, R: DeserializeOwned, F: Fn() -> Fut, Fut: Future<Output = Result<Box<dyn GuestConnection>, HostError>>;
      /// Forget the guest for `key` and close it in the background of the caller.
      pub async fn abandon(&self, key: &K);
  }
  ```
  One lock guards the map only; each slot has its own lock around its `Session`, so a slow provider does not block another. A second failure after the retry evicts and returns `CallError::Failed`.
